proof.text:
For the two projection maps just used, [def-exchange-projection] defines $\pi_{u;V,W}=u_*a_{u,V,W}\circ\eta_u$, where, after the monoidal comparison, $a_{u,V,W}=\varepsilon_{u,V}\otimes1_{u^*W}$. Hence naturality of the counit and the triangle identity in [fix-prop-adjunctions](1) give directly
$$\varepsilon_{u,V\otimes u^*W}\circ u^*\pi_{u;V,W}
=a_{u,V,W}\circ\varepsilon_{u,u^*(u_*V\otimes W)}\circ u^*\eta_{u,u_*V\otimes W}
=a_{u,V,W}.$$
Use this formula only with $(u,V,W)=(g,N,F)$ and $(q,H,N)$. Each is an evaluation of the definition, followed by one triangle cancellation; no projection theorem beyond the identifications in Step 1 is being inferred.
